FILED s543p (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27, CODE 0ab08642 = MAIN-READY-111, v2-16300) by the Rosetta census (docs/rosetta-plan.md step 1; #2104).

THE SHAPE (neutral reproducer, run on the tree, perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):

    my $s = "abcabc";
    print $s =~ s/\Ga/X/r, "\n";        # perl Xbcabc    PCL abcabc
    pos($s) = 3;
    print $s =~ s/\Ga/X/r, "\n";        # perl abcXbc    PCL abcabc
    pos($s) = 2;
    print $s =~ s/\G.*//r, "|\n";       # perl ab|       PCL abcabc|
    my $g = "Gab";
    print $g =~ s/\Ga/X/r, "\n";        # perl Gab       PCL Xb   <- \G read as a literal G

perl: `\G` in a substitution anchors at the target's pos() (0 when unset), as in a match; with /g it anchors each step at the previous step's end.  PCL: the in-place, /r and /g spellings all miss.

WHERE: the match operator's compile step strips `\G` (`%pcl-strip-g`, cl/pcl-runtime.lisp ~43277: "cl-ppcre has no \G") and requires the match to start at pos; the `p-subst` path (`(p-subst :pat "\\Ga" :rep "X" ...)`) does not go through it, so cl-ppcre sees `\G` and reads it as the letter G.

CHEAP DISCRIMINATING MEASUREMENT (taken): the "Gab" row above -- PCL replaces "Ga", so the pattern reached cl-ppcre with the `\G` un-stripped (not a wrong pos).

THE PROGRAM: 0071-Arithmetic-evaluation: its error routine prints the input up to the failure point by deleting from `\G` to the end with a `/r` substitution, so every error line's caret column is wrong (the whole line kept).  0071 also needs #5460.

=== s543p (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27, CODE 496df8b1 = MAIN-READY-113) === Rosetta 0996-Peaceful-chess-queen-armies holds this cause too: inside a `while (/-/g)` loop it replaces the character JUST BEFORE pos with a `/r` substitution whose pattern ends in `\G` (a backtracking search that places one piece per step); PCL never matches, places nothing and reports no solution.
NEUTRAL REPRODUCER (run on the tree):
    my $s = "a-b-c";
    while ($s =~ /-/g) {
      print $s =~ s/-\G/+/r, "\n";
    }
  perl: a+b-c / a-b+c        PCL: a-b-c / a-b-c
Rewriting that one substitution as a 4-argument substr at pos-1 makes 0996 identical to perl -- its only cause.
LABEL: silent (ordinary: Rosetta 0071, 0996)

=== s543q (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-28, CODE 6a1301ed) ===
ONE MORE ROSETTA PROGRAM: 1297-Solve-a-Hopido-puzzle (census B, LOUD: the search never succeeds and the program dies with its own "no solution" message).  A recursive solver finds the next free cell with a lookahead match `/.../g` (pos set) and builds the next board with `s/\G00/$new/r`; under PCL the `\G` is a literal G, the substitution never fires, so no board ever changes.  Patching only the eight `s/\G00/$new/r` sites to `substr($copy, pos(), 2, $new)` makes the program byte-identical to perl: this task is its only stdout cause (its `(local $_, my $last) = @_;` is #3414's announced shape and does not change stdout).
Neutral reproducer, run on the tree:
    $_ = "q00r00";
    /r(?=00)/g and print s/\G00/X/r, "\n";
    perl: q00rX
    PCL : q00r00


=== DONE (s543u) ===
\G is a mark the parse tree makes a zero-width filter on *p-gpos*, which every op binds: the target's pos() (0 unset) for a single match, s/// and the first //g / s///g step, each later step's start.  m//'s leading-\G fast path kept (anchored kind); %pcl-strip-gpos deleted (it also stripped non-leading \G: /-\G/, /\Ga|b/, (?:\Ga)+ were wrong in m// too).  Kinds: anchored, leading (gofs 0: Pod::Simple's m{(?:\A|\G/)...}g), floating (scan from 0, end >= pos, start+gofs==end is zero-length), partial (refused under //g: X\G|b; s///g stops where perl's REXEC_FAIL_ON_UNDERFLOW does, t/re/subst.t's s/bc|(.)\G(.)/../ge).  Probes p2-gpos 30/30, p2b 19/20 (the refusal), p2c 7/7.  Guards rows 73-75.  ROSETTA: 547 -> 563 of 650 (scratch/s543u/rosetta-1.log; NEW 0 FIXED 0 UNEXPLAINED 0 STALE 0).  0996 1297 0071 same.  ir-spec Â§10-gpos.
